    "lawCode": "Amd §33-0303, En Con L; amd §§70 & 172, rpld §71, Nav L",
    "lawSection": "Environmental Conservation Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S5197\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act to amend the environmental conservation law and the navigation\nlaw, in relation to consideration of environmental conditions when\npermitting petroleum-bearing vessels to enter navigable waters; and\nrepealing section seventy-one of the navigation law relating to the\npetroleum-bearing vessel advisory commission\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nTo update the factors used to determine the conditions under which\npetroleum-bearing vessels may enter or move upon navigable waters of\nthe state, as well as for establishing tanker-avoidance zones.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1: Adds a new subdivision to section 33-0303 of the\nenvironmental conservation law relating to the powers and duties of\nthe commissioner regarding the guidelines for the establishment of\nconditions for petroleum-bearing vessels to enter or move upon\nnavigable waters of the state, as well as tanker-avoidance zones.\n\nSection 2: Amends section 70 of the navigation law to provide that the\nCommissioner of the NYS Department of Environmental Conservation may\nalso work in consultation with the Department of State and the Office\nof Parks, Recreation and Historic Preservation with regards to the\nestablishment of conditions for petroleum-bearing vessels to enter or\nmove upon navigable waters of the state, as well as tanker-avoidance\nzones. Adds that environmental conditions such as the existence of\ndesignated significant coastal fish and wildlife habitats and\nproximity to waterfront communities shall be considered when making\nsuch considerations. Also removes reference to the petroleum-bearing\nvessel advisory commission.\n\nSection 3: Repeals section 71 of the navigation law relating to the\npetroleum-bearing, vessel advisory commission.\n\nSection 4: Amends section 172 of the navigation law to add tank\nvessels, barges and tug-barge combinations to the definition of\n\"petroleum-bearing vessel.\"\n\nSection 5: Establishes the effective date.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nThe United States Coast Guard issued an Advance Notice of Proposed\nRulemaking to establish 10 new anchorage grounds which could\npotentially create 43 new vessel berths in the Hudson River between\nKingston and Yonkers. The proposed plan raises economic and health and\nsafety concerns and it is important that New York State is able to\ntake appropriate factors into account when determining the use of its\nnavigable waters.\n\nThe Hudson River and surrounding waterfronts are the lifeblood of the\ncommunities through which it passes, and members of these communities\nhave expressed their fear that, in addition to potential accidents,\ntheir scenic waterfronts could be transformed into parking lots for\nunsightly barges. This legislation will enhance the State's ability to\nprotect its communities and to preserve the natural integrity of the\nregion.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNew bill.\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
