    "lawCode": "Amd §3-0301, En Con L; add §70-a, amd §2, Nav L",
    "lawSection": "Navigation Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S5197A\n\n TITLE OF BILL :  An act to amend the environmental conservation law\nand the navigation law, in relation to consideration of environmental\nconditions when permitting petroleum-bearing vessels to enter\nnavigable waters\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nTo establish factors used to determine the conditions under which\npetroleum-bearing vessels may enter or move upon navigable waters of\nthe Hudson River, as well as for establishing tanker-avoidance zones\nalong the river.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1: Amends subdivision 2 of section 3-0301 of the environmental\nconservation law relating to the powers and duties of the commissioner\nregarding the guidelines for the establishment of conditions for\npetroleum-bearing vessels to enter or move upon navigable waters of\nthe state, as well as tanker-avoidance zones.\n\nSection 2: Adds a new section 70-a of the navigation law to provide\nthat the Commissioner of the NYS Department of Environmental\nConservation may work in consultation with the United States Coast\nGuard, the Board of Commissioners of Pilots, the Department of State,\nthe Office of Parks, Recreation and Historic Preservation and at least\none licensed Hudson River Pilot with regards to the establishment\nguidelines setting forth the conditions for petroleum-bearing vessels\nto enter or move upon navigable waters of the Hudson River, as well as\ntanker-avoidance zones. Also adds conditions that may be considered\nfor such guidelines, and requires the Commissioner of Environmental\nConservation, in consultation with those referenced above, to submit a\nreport on any proposed rulemaking from the United States Coast Guard\nthat would impact the Hudson River within 120 days of this act taking\neffect.\n\nSection 3: Adds a new subdivision 4-a to section 2 of the navigation\nlaw to define \"Navigable waters of the Hudson river.\"\n\nSection 4: Establishes the effective date.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nThe United States Coast Guard issued an Advance Notice of Proposed\nRulemaking to establish 10 new anchorage grounds which could\npotentially create 43 new vessel berths in the Hudson River between\nKingston and Yonkers. The proposed plan raises economic and health and\nsafety concerns and it is important that New York State is able to\ntake appropriate factors into account when determining the use of its\nnavigable waters.\n\nThe Hudson River and surrounding waterfronts are the lifeblood of the\ncommunities through which it passes, and members of these communities\nhave expressed their fear that, in addition to potential accidents,\ntheir scenic waterfronts could be transformed into parking lots for\nunsightly barges. This legislation will enhance the State's ability to\nprotect its communities and to preserve the natural integrity of the\nregion.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNew bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
